15 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Two line graphs depict canopy relative humidity, temperature, and dew point over time. The left graph shows relative humidity between thirty-seven and fifty-eight percent, temperature between seven and twenty-three degrees Celsius, and dew point between eight and nine degrees Celsius over fourteen weeks. The right graph displays relative humidity between seventy-eight and ninety-eight percent, temperature between twenty-one and twenty-three degrees Celsius, and dew point between nineteen and twenty degrees Celsius over fifteen weeks. Each variable is represented by a different symbol.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Two bar charts comparing plant growth metrics at different relative humidity \(RH\) levels. Chart \(A\) shows plant biomass categories: fresh weight, dry weight, flowers plus leaves, flowers, and roots. Plants under lower RH \(78-98%\) generally show lower biomass compared to low RH \(37-58%\). Chart \(B\) depicts plant structures: stem length, trunk diameter, apical internode, and nodes. lower RH conditions lead to decreased measurements, except for apical internode, where low RH shows similar or higher values. Statistical significance is indicated by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Two-panel image showing cannabis plants under different conditions. Panel A displays a cannabis plant in purple light with 37-58% relative humidity. Panel B shows another plant in purple light with 78-98% relative humidity. Below, Cannabis plants showing different height at low and high RH levels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing the number of branches bearing inflorescence from weeks 10 to 15 for Cherry Berry plants. Light blue bars represent low relative humidity \(RH\) of 37-58%, and dark blue bars represent high RH of 78-98%. Weeks 13 and 14 show significant differences between low and high RH, with higher values in low RH conditions. Insets show close-up images of inflorescence under low and high RH conditions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Bar charts showing cannabinoid content under different relative humidity \(RH\) levels. Panel A: Cannabinoid content in milligrams per gram with lower levels at RH 78-98%. Panel B: Total cannabinoid content in percentage, again lower at RH 78-98%. Panel C: Cannabinoid ratios, notably CBD:THC with a significant decrease at higher RH. Data indicates impact of humidity on cannabinoid content and ratios.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
